            "lens": "review-risk",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "The goal filter in the Engram SQL uses a bound placeholder for the goal id and a fixed prefix literal built from a constant. Goal input never reaches the SQL text, so there is no injection path. The test in longterm-mem/internal/engram/search_goal_test.go covers goal ids containing _, %, and /.",
              "PageTagReader in longterm-mem/internal/vault/pagetags.go resolves symlinks on both the page path and the vault root, and rejects relative paths and paths outside the root. Tests in longterm-mem/internal/vault/pagetags_test.go cover an outside page, a symlink to an outside file, and a symlink to an outside directory. There is no arbitrary file read, and only frontmatter tags are returned.",
              "Under a goal, the vault source fails closed: pages whose tags cannot be read are left out and named in a diagnostic. This is in longterm-mem/internal/query/vault_goal.go. The diagnostic includes page addresses and error text from paths under the vault root, which is minor and not a reachable exposure.",
              "The vault over-fetch is capped by VaultGoalCandidateBound (100), so the extra work stays bounded.",
              "Without a goal, every path behaves as before. Search is called with an empty filter, the vault is asked for top candidates, and no tags are read.",
              "No dependency or lockfile changes, and no secrets are introduced."
            ]
          }
        }
