            "lens": "review-reliability",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "The SQL goal clause in longterm-mem/internal/engram/search.go compares the parsed goal id and is applied before LIMIT. TestSearch_UnderAGoalKeepsThatGoalAndNoGoal checks it against memory.TopicVisibleUnderGoal for edge topics (empty id, no slash, '_' and '%' in the goal, a goal containing '/'). TestSearch_UnderAGoalHoldsTheRankOrderAndTheLimit checks that rank order and the limit are preserved.",
              "The embedding arm filters on topic before the cut at top, and the vault arm over-fetches (bounded at 100) and filters on tags. Pages whose tags cannot be read are left out and named in a diagnostic. With no goal the retrieval is unchanged, which the tests assert (vault asked for top, no tag reads).",
              "The tag reader rejects relative paths and paths outside the vault, including through symlinks, and rejects unclosed frontmatter and unclosed flow lists. Its tests cover each of these cases.",
              "The change threads Goal through the CLI flag, the MCP argument, and the query request. Tests assert the forwarding, and the golden schema was updated. Promotion and skill-candidate topic rules now read the topic with the goal prefix removed, and tests cover that.",
              "I found no reliability defect in the visible patch. I could not check callers of Search outside the patch, because the patch is the only view of the candidate."
            ]
          }
        }
